<!-- ── §07 Reference Pipeline ────────────────────────────────── -->
<section id="s-pipeline" data-code="pipeline">
<div class="section-no">07 — Reference Pipeline</div>
<h2>A CI/CD Pipeline You Can Wire Up Today</h2>

<p>Here's a concrete five-stage pipeline that teams use in production. Each stage has a clear trigger, a bounded runtime, and a specific gate criterion. Walk through the stages:</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">Reference LLM CI/CD pipeline — 5 stages from commit to production</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">Prev / Next through each stage</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <div class="step-list" id="pipe-list">

      <div class="step-box active" id="pipe-0">
        <div class="step-num">1</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="tier-pills">
            <span class="tier-pill tp-fast">trigger: git push</span>
            <span class="tier-pill tp-fast">&lt; 30 seconds</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-title">Stage 1 — Assertion Gate</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Run all Tier 1 assertion evals. Check: JSON validity, response length, no forbidden strings, latency under SLA. Zero LLM calls. This catches hard failures instantly and blocks broken prompts from wasting Tier 2 budget.</div>
          <div class="step-code">deepeval test run tests/tier1_assertions.py --min-success-rate 1.0</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-box" id="pipe-1">
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="tier-pills">
            <span class="tier-pill tp-mid">trigger: PR open</span>
            <span class="tier-pill tp-mid">2–8 minutes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-title">Stage 2 — LLM-as-Judge on Golden Dataset</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Run the full golden dataset (50–200 examples) through both baseline and candidate. Judge LLM scores each response on Faithfulness, Helpfulness, Safety. Compute delta against baseline scores. Post results as a PR comment.</div>
          <div class="step-code">results = evaluator.compare(
    baseline=baseline_version,
    candidate=pr_branch,
    dataset=golden_dataset_v3,
    metrics=["faithfulness", "helpfulness", "safety"]
)
# Gate: candidate must not regress on ANY metric by &gt;2%</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-box" id="pipe-2">
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="tier-pills">
            <span class="tier-pill tp-mid">trigger: merge to main</span>
            <span class="tier-pill tp-mid">auto-decision</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-title">Stage 3 — Threshold Gate</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Candidate scores must meet absolute thresholds (not just beat baseline). If baseline has degraded over time, you don't want to use it as floor. Hard minimums: Faithfulness ≥ 0.85, Helpfulness ≥ 0.80, Hallucination rate ≤ 10%.</div>
          <div class="step-code">if results.faithfulness &lt; 0.85 or results.hallucination_rate &gt; 0.10:
    block_deploy(reason=results.summary())
    notify_slack("#llm-releases", results)
else:
    promote_to_staging()</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-box" id="pipe-3">
        <div class="step-num">4</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="tier-pills">
            <span class="tier-pill tp-slow">trigger: staging approval</span>
            <span class="tier-pill tp-slow">canary: 5% traffic</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-title">Stage 4 — Shadow &amp; Canary Deploy</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Route 5% of production traffic to the candidate. Monitor real latency, error rates, and implicit feedback (re-prompts, session abandonment). If metrics hold for 24h, ramp to 50%, then 100%. Rollback is one command.</div>
          <div class="step-code">deploy.canary(
    version=candidate,
    traffic_pct=5,
    success_criteria=&#123;"p95_latency_ms": 2000, "error_rate": 0.01&#125;,
    rollback_on_breach=True,
    ramp_schedule=[5, 25, 100],
    ramp_interval_hours=24
)</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-box" id="pipe-4">
        <div class="step-num">5</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="tier-pills">
            <span class="tier-pill tp-fast">continuous</span>
            <span class="tier-pill tp-fast">feeds next cycle</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-title">Stage 5 — Production Monitoring → Golden Dataset</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Sample production traffic (bias toward failures, low-confidence outputs, user re-prompts). Review daily. Add confirmed failures to golden dataset. Version the dataset. This closes the flywheel and makes the next deployment cycle cheaper.</div>
          <div class="step-code">sampler.run(
    strategy="failure_biased",         # oversample bad outcomes
    sample_rate=&#123;"failure": 0.30, "success": 0.02&#125;,
    review_queue="llm-quality-review",
    auto_add_threshold=0.40             # auto-add if judge score &lt; 0.40
)</div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
